80 golden questions, 1,454 chunks, recall@5 of the verified chunk

  vectors stored as                  bytes each  recall@5  same top 5
  32-bit floats (full)                    6,144       59%        100%
  8-bit integers                          1,536       59%         96%
  1 bit per dimension                       192       62%         57%
  1 bit, then rescore top 50 in full        192       59%        100%

Recall alone hides what one bit did: it held at 62% on 80 questions while only 57% of
each top five stayed the same. The right chunk survived, its neighbours changed, and
whether that costs recall is a question for a much larger set than this one.

A bit per dimension is 32 times smaller than the full vector. On its own it reorders the
top results; used as a first pass, with the shortlist rescored against full vectors kept
on disk, it gives back the full ranking for a fraction of the memory.
